{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-28T05:24:41.761Z","author":"pm-github","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-6.2-sol","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"6158739a7b0750be95903009","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-6.2-sol","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"high","source":"probe"},"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/body","value":"Found while reviewing the pull request that fixes issue 287 (repeat-import no-op). That pull request restored Projects push to main's behaviour to keep its scope, so both defects remain on main.\n\n\nWith one native item and an empty board, build two push plans before either applies. Applying both produces two remote drafts and two board tags on the same item. Separately, let `addProjectV2DraftIssue` return a card ID and reject `updateProjectV2ItemFieldValue`. Current `main` reports `Sync wrote nothing; 1 operation(s) failed.` after the provider has accepted the attachment. The previous PR implementation returned `pushed: 1, pushFailed: 0` in JSON for that same partial outcome.\n\nBefore attachment, revalidate the live board and complete tracker binding, including tags for cards absent from the original snapshot. Preserve or reconcile the confirmed card ID before retrying. Expose attachment, status, and tracker-tag results in JSON and TOON with an explicit partial outcome. Add real non-git tracker tests proving that two stale plans yield one card and one tag, and that a status refusal remains visible while retry reuses the attached card."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-github-github-ee4d59c27b67-303"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"Projects push: fence stale attachment plans and report partial outcomes (duplicate drafts; a rejected status write after an accepted attachment reports nothing written)"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"GH issue #303: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-github/issues/303 · author @unbraind · created 2026-11-28T01:50:33Z · updated 2026-11-28T01:50:56Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["gh:unbraind/pm-github#303","github_author:unbraind"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-11-28T05:24:41.761Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-28T05:24:41.761Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"pm-github"}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"5ffb046cf070205a656fc7a8873eba0e28667bbf48f33c65309589132389fed7","item_hash_version":3,"message":"Imported from GitHub #303","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"effort":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"unavailable","reason":"harness_unavailable","resolver":"ai_agent_version","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"9222a22381ce30a6092934c3b6122feb1876186aab02f6500c19e4e94dd7ab77"}
